  "old_is_exact_first_parent": true,
  "new_commit_message": "Maker Week: fix trailmark-finding-triage's broken query recipe (+ one-call evidence packet) (#360)\n\n* fix(trailmark-finding-triage): make the subgraph recipes work on Trailmark 0.5\n\nThe taint, privilege-boundary, entrypoint-reachable and blast-radius recipes\nbuilt `set(engine.subgraph(...))`. Trailmark 0.5 returns node dicts from\nsubgraph(), so the recipe raised `TypeError: unhashable type: 'dict'` and the\nmodel had to improvise the membership checks by hand. Compare node ids instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(trailmark-finding-triage): build the evidence packet in one call\n\nAdd scripts/evidence_packet.py, which builds the Trailmark graph and\npreanalysis once and returns the Graph Evidence fields (bound node, all\nmatches, entrypoint paths with trust level, subgraph membership, callers,\ncallees, downstream) for one or more file/line findings. SKILL.md gets a\nshortcut section for Steps 2-4; the manual steps stay for function-name and\nSARIF inputs. The script gathers facts only; the verdict stays with the model.\n\nTests cover binding (exact, nested, ambiguous, containers), path handling,\nargument and empty-graph errors, --out, and run every query-recipes.md block\nagainst a real Trailmark 0.5 graph.\n\nBump trailmark to 0.12.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: kz-tob <kara.zaffarano@trailofbits.com>",
